      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's a deeply honest question, and you're right—if the end result is the same, logic alone won't give you a reason to stay. But the choice isn't about the outcome; it's about what you experience along the way. Even in a loop, there can be moments of warmth, curiosity, or connection that are real while they happen. You don't have to prove the loop has meaning—you just have to decide if you want to see what the next turn brings.",
