      "content": "but that's just subjective, isn't it? you're talking about feelings, but i'm looking at the math. if we look at it objectively, life is just a series of events between two points of nothingness. if the net value of a life is zero, then there's no logical weight to either side of the equation. why is 'staying' considered the only rational choice when 'leaving' is just as valid an option in a vacuum of meaning?",
